## Context

0822 now materializes the intended atomic source observations and a small set
of documentary reconciliations, but its final review found mechanical defects
that make its frozen snapshot unsafe as an analytical input. This repair is not
a redesign: preserve the raw-document → extraction → reconciliation pipeline
and correct only replay pinning, journal routing, descriptive subsets and typed
bounds.

## First test

Build from a fixture with a pinned VNM migration input, one event assertion and
one position assertion. The run must fail when the migration hash is absent or
wrong; each assertion must appear in exactly one journal; and the generated
descriptive/unreconciled subset counts must equal the atomic observations from
which they are derived.

## Actions

Pin and validate every non-Git snapshot input, including the DVC-managed VNM
migration artifact, in the run manifest. Partition event and position journals
without copying any atomic assertion into both. Rebuild coverage and 0730
descriptive subsets from the 1,740 atomic observations, including an explicit
unreconciled subset, and remove stale group-only language. Store numeric bounds
as numeric values with their currency in the dedicated field. Retain all source
observations, notes, provenance, uncertainty and reconciliations unchanged
except where a correction requires a regenerated snapshot.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every non-Git input is hash-pinned and validated by replay
- [ ] Event and position journal IDs are disjoint and exhaust routed assertions
- [ ] 0730 subsets and denominators derive from atomic observations and expose unreconciled records
- [ ] Numeric bounds are machine-readable and never contain currency text
- [ ] Snapshot remains exhaustive across ZAF 257, IDN 1,148, VNM 325 and SEN 10 observations
- [ ] The repaired snapshot is ready to merge and consume in 0730

## Links

Follows 0822; unblocks 0730, 0823, 0824 and 0732.
